70. The security controls to be implemented at HSM are:
The HSMs should have logging enabled, the logs must themselves be tamper proof;
HSM can become a single point of failure. This needs to be mitigated by ‘clustering’ for high availability and ensure secure backups;
Access to the HSM should be controlled through Access Control Lists (ACLs);

